| $\\,3.490\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Since $X∼{χ}^{2}(7),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=7.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $\\,0.989\\,$ | $\\,1.239\\,$ | $\\,1.690\\,$ | $\\,2.167\\,$ | $\\,2.833\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>1.690)=0.975.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=1.690.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec19c717-37bc-53c3-b09e-21a2fd2b77fa" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Chi-Square Probability Using the Complement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b9b65f2-32b1-5306-a674-1a8cce394049" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.711" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492344} {:answer/id #uuid "487a0cb4-3b3c-53b1-ad75-19be1635b445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492362} {:answer/id #uuid "760efcf4-e371-5ee5-8095-2afc058abad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.072" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492455} {:answer/id #uuid "801fb805-5abf-578a-bed5-8eed93de26a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.412" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492473} {:answer/id #uuid "d6fc4ad5-887a-55cb-91ae-8042270e76d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.207" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6fc4ad5-887a-55cb-91ae-8042270e76d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.207" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492640} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccb2367b-54fc-50aa-8684-3aa2a710859d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1169ae0-dbcc-5afc-b27c-5d1844b9830b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108271" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$ Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X\\le x)=0.005.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $\\,0.072\\,$ | $\\,0.115\\,$ | $\\,0.216\\,$ | $\\,0.352\\,$ | $\\,0.584\\,$ |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The table shows probabilities in the form $P(X>x).$ So first, we express the desired probability in this form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>x) & =1-P(X\\le x) \\\\  & =1-0.005 \\\\  & =0.995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $X∼{χ}^{2}(4),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=4.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>0.207)=0.995.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=0.207.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161926 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a75e6c3-16e3-50ab-bd36-a2c83ba9288a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Probability Involving Sums of Squared Standard Normal Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5731441f-975d-55af-aa2c-666c2201d3f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60.346" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5731441f-975d-55af-aa2c-666c2201d3f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60.346" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492382} :answer-field/id #uuid "346fec95-da88-5e3b-8992-afee68fefadc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c65221c-bb24-5314-9566-2deac5724c52" :question/math-academy-id "q-252041" :question/problem "Let the random variable $Y$ be defined as\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{50}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le 50.$ Find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\le y)=0.85.$\n\n*Hint: The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $48$ | $\\,73.683\\,$ | $\\,65.171\\,$ | $\\,60.907\\,$ | $\\,58.135\\,$ | $\\,55.993\\,$ |\n| $49$ | $\\,74.919\\,$ | $\\,66.339\\,$ | $\\,62.038\\,$ | $\\,59.241\\,$ | $\\,57.079\\,$ |\n| $50$ | $\\,76.154\\,$ | $\\,67.505\\,$ | $\\,63.167\\,$ | $\\,60.346\\,$ | $\\,58.164\\,$ |\n\nThe value of $y$ that satisfies $P(Y\\le y)=0.85$ is $y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "If ${Z}_{i}∼N(0,1)$ for $1\\le i\\le k$ are independent normal random variables, then the sum\n\n$$\n{Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{k}^{2}\n$$\n\nfollows a ${χ}^{2}(k)$ distribution with $k$ degrees of freedom.\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\nY={Z}_{1}^{2}+{Z}_{2}^{2}+⋯+{Z}_{50}^{2}∼{χ}^{2}(50).\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the given probability in the form $P(Y\\ge y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le y) & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ 0.85 & =1-P(Y\\ge y) \\\\ P(Y\\ge y) & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we wish to find the value $y$ such that $P(Y\\ge y)=0.15$ This can be found from the given table:\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.100$ | $0.150$ | $0.200$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $48$ | $\\,73.683\\,$ | $\\,65.171\\,$ | $\\,60.907\\,$ | $\\,58.135\\,$ | $\\,55.993\\,$ |\n| $49$ | $\\,74.919\\,$ | $\\,66.339\\,$ | $\\,62.038\\,$ | $\\,59.241\\,$ | $\\,57.079\\,$ |\n| $50$ | $\\,76.154\\,$ | $\\,67.505\\,$ | $\\,63.167\\,$ | $\\,60.346\\,$ | $\\,58.164\\,$ |\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y\\ge 60.346)=0.15\n$$\n\nwhich means\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le 60.346)=0.85.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=60.346.$"}]}
